{{also|Blob|BLOB}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/blɒb/|a=UK}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɒb|s=1}}
* {{IPA|en|/blɑb/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-blob.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|BLOB}}

===Etymology 1===
Possibly {{onomatopoeic|en|nocap=1}}, similarly to {{m|en|bleb}} and {{m|en|blubber}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A shapeless or [[amorphous]] mass; a [[vague]] [[shape]] or [[amount]], especially of a liquid or semisolid substance; a [[clump]], [[group]] or [[collection]] that lacks definite shape.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1869|author=Norman Lockyer; et al|title=Nature
|passage=Only the outermost '''blob''' on either side in map 2 displays misalignment.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1895|title=The Annual of the British School at Athens
|passage=It was a colourful vase with red and white hoops on the lid, and red bands above and below the main [[frieze]]. These bands also carry a [[metope]] pattern in white of triple lines and '''blobs''', which can just be distinguished on the photographs.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1922|author=w:Virginia Woolf|title=w:Jacob's Room|chapter=1|passage=But there, on the very top, is a hollow full of water, with a sandy bottom; with a '''blob''' of jelly stuck to the side, and some mussels.}}
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} A large cloud of gas.
## {{ellipsis of|en|[[extended]] [[Lyman-Alpha]] [[blob]]|nodot=1}} {{gloss|a huge body of gas that may be the precursor to a galaxy}}.<ref>[http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2009/04/090422151828.htm]</ref>
# {{lb|en|dialect}} A [[bubble]]; a [[bleb]].
# A small [[freshwater]] [[fish]] ({{taxlink|Cottus bairdii|species}}); the miller's thumb.<!--Webster 1913-->
# The partially inflated air bag used in the sport of [[blobbing]].
# {{lb|en|sports|slang}} A [[score]] of [[zero]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1925|title=Punch|volume=168|page=561
|passage=A gentleman named W. Shakespeare scored a '''blob''' in the Worcestershire v. Lancashire match. We understand that he got out because the ball pitched on a "damned spot."}}

